### When exception Occur
NullPointerException
When it occurs:
➡️ When you try to access a method or variable of a null object
Example:
String s = null;
System.out.println(s.length());
Reason:
➡️ The object does not exist (reference is null)
ArithmeticException
When it occurs:
➡️ When an invalid arithmetic operation happens (usually division by zero)
Example:
int a = 10 / 0;
Reason:
➡️ Division by zero is not allowed
One-line memory trick
NullPointerException → Object is null
ArithmeticException → Math operation is wrong
